.Dd November 12, 2026
.Dt VFSD 8
.Os RavenBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm vfsd
.Nd file namespace server and mount table
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm /sbin/vfsd
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
owns the scheme
.Dq file:
and presents the mounted filesystem servers as one absolute tree
.Pq Pa / .
It reads
.Pa /etc/mounts
through the
.Dq initfs:
scheme, waits for each listed scheme to appear, mounts it and then registers
.Dq file: .
.Pp
Each line of
.Pa /etc/mounts
is one
.Dq Aq path Aq scheme
pair.  Paths must be absolute and normalized; blank lines and
.Ql #
comments are ignored.  The compiled-in defaults are:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
/          initfs:
/tmp       ramfs:
/dev/null  null:
/dev/zero  zero:
/dev/random rand:
.Ed
.Pp
A missing optional mount is logged and skipped; a missing
.Pa /
is fatal.
.Pp
For
.Dv OPEN ,
.Nm
normalizes the path, chooses the longest whole-component mount prefix and opens
the path on the owning server.  The owning server's handle is returned as an S25
reply attachment, so subsequent reads and writes go directly to that server.
Path operations
.Pq Dv MKDIR , UNLINK , RMDIR , RENAME , TRUNCATE , SYMLINK , READLINK , CHMOD
are forwarded as
.Dv CALL
requests; a rename across mounts returns
.Er EXDEV .
.Dv MOUNT
and
.Dv UMOUNT
are handled locally.
.Dv SYNC
is forwarded to every mount and
.Dv STATFS
to the root mount.
.Pp
The root
.Dq file:
handle is kept by
.Nm
so that
.Dv READ
on
.Pa /
merges the root server's entries with the names of mounts directly below
.Pa /
\(em for example
.Pa /tmp
\(em without duplicating a name.  Other opens are attachments.
.Pp
Limits: 32 mounts, paths no longer than 255 bytes, and one forwarded
.Dv CALL
at a time per server thread.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /etc/services.d/vfsd.toml -compact
.It Pa /etc/mounts
mount table
.It Pa /etc/services.d/vfsd.toml
service manifest
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr open 2 ,
.Xr ramfsd 8
.Sh STANDARDS
RavenBSD ABI v1.
